# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-install-missing-cad-runtime-lsp — installed alfe cannot find its CAD runtime LSP assets
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-install-cad-runtime-lsp

* Context

The alfe AutoCAD/BricsCAD backends stage two runtime assets into the engine
workdir before launching the CAD engine:

- =autolisp-bootstrap.lsp= — defines the autolisp-* helpers the runtime
  server loop calls;
- =autolisp-remote-io.lsp= — the CAD-side runtime the bridge loads.

=DISCOVER-BOOTSTRAP-LSP= / =DISCOVER-RUNTIME-LSP= (backend-cad-common.lisp)
resolve them in this order:

1. =$ALFE_BOOTSTRAP_LSP= / =$ALFE_RUNTIME_LSP= (when set and the file exists);
2. the *vendored* copy under =source/runtime/= next to the code;
3. the fallback search list — first entry =$PREFIX/share/alfe/runtime/=.

* Problem

On an *installed* system all three fail:

- the env vars are unset;
- a dumped SBCL image (=alfe-sbcl.exe=) has no source tree beside it, so the
  vendored copy resolves to nothing;
- =autolisp-front-end/Makefile='s =install= / =install-programs= only ever
  installed =bin/=, =libexec/= and =share/{doc,info,man}= — it NEVER installed
  the two assets to =$PREFIX/share/alfe/runtime/=, the very location the
  fallback list points at.

Reproduced on a real Windows + AutoCAD 2022 host with a clean
=clautolisp-1.9.3-all.zip= install (Aug 2026):

#+begin_example
$ alfe -norc --autocad --cad acad-2022 --mode automation --dwg empty.dwg \
       --keep-workdir --print-command
alfe[warn]: backend AUTOCAD: no bootstrap LSP found; set $ALFE_BOOTSTRAP_LSP or install autolisp-bootstrap.lsp
alfe[warn]: backend AUTOCAD: no runtime LSP found; set $ALFE_RUNTIME_LSP or install autolisp-remote-io.lsp
#+end_example

The assets shipped ONLY inside the source copy the release also installs
(=$PREFIX/src/clautolisp-<v>/autolisp-front-end/source/runtime/=), which is
not on the search path. So the AutoCAD/BricsCAD automation and batch backends
cannot bootstrap on any installed system — the reason the CAD automation path
had never run end to end from an install.

* Fix (clautolisp 1.9.6)

=autolisp-front-end/Makefile=: =install-programs= now installs both assets to
=$(PREFIX)/share/alfe/runtime/= (a new =RUNTIME_INSTALL_DIR=), and =uninstall=
removes them. The path is =share/alfe/runtime= (not =share/autolisp-front-end=)
to match =*bootstrap-lsp-fallback-paths*= / =*runtime-lsp-fallback-paths*=
exactly.

Verified: =make -C autolisp-front-end install-programs DESTDIR=… PREFIX=/opt/local=
lands both files under =…/opt/local/share/alfe/runtime/=.

* Acceptance criteria

- [X] An installed alfe (env vars unset, dumped image) resolves both runtime
  assets via the =$PREFIX/share/alfe/runtime/= fallback — no "no bootstrap/
  runtime LSP found" warnings.
- [X] =uninstall= removes them.
- [ ] End-to-end AutoCAD automation reaching READY on the Windows runner —
  tracked separately, and additionally blocked by
  [[alfe-release-ships-stale-image]] (the 1.9.3-all.zip shipped a stale alfe
  image that also crashes on ALFE.BACKEND.AUTOCAD::PROBE).
